{
  "abstract": "We prove the rational Hodge conjecture for every self-power of the K3 surface $Y^2=X^3+6aUX+2U(2U-a^3)$, where $U=D_5(s)-2$ and $a$ is any complex parameter. Its generic Picard number is 14 and its transcendental endomorphism field is $\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt5)$. The geometric input is an explicit degree-120 rational map from the square of the genus-19 cyclic curve $w^{30}=v^{26}(1-v)^{15}(1-\\lambda v)^5$, with $a^3=-2(\\lambda-1)^2/\\lambda$. The transcendental image lies in the primitive abelian eightfold factor of its Jacobian. Four independent Gauss monodromies determine the generic derived group. Transporting the K3 pairing and applying an explicit rational projector constructs all four quartic-CM Weil classes. A second degree-60 quotient realizes the full determinant variation on the fixed surface $y^2=x^3+Q^4(1-Q^5)^2$. This surface is dominated by CM elliptic curves with fields $\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt{-3})$ and $\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt{-15})$. Invariant theory and algebraic transfer prove HC on mixed products of these elliptic curves, source eightfolds and K3 surfaces at any finite list of non-CM source parameters. Shared determinants turn linked derived factors into algebraic isogenies. André--Oort makes the excluded parameter set finite. Specialization of real-quadratic volume classes handles the remaining K3 parameters; the four source Weil classes also specialize to every smooth fiber. We credit the existing Dickson multiplication, Varesco's extraction and specialization mechanisms, and the elliptic-product Hodge theorem. Six exact CPU certificates verify the displayed algebra and character inputs. Full HC for every source of CM type, generic canonical Kuga-Satake algebraicity and general rational HC remain unresolved.",
